-1.  **Initialization Pass:** Render sections of the volume that are *not* enclosed within any translucent geometry. This pass initializes the front and back accumulation buffers with the colors of the volume parts visible outside the geometry [S1, unofficial].
-2.  **Geometry Peeling Pass:** Perform a dual depth peeling pass on the translucent geometry. This computes the color and depth of the front and back layers (peels) of the geometry in a single render pass. The computed colors are accumulated in separate geometry buffers, and the updated depths are stored to feed the next pair of peels [S1, unofficial].
